<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">elite-pathfinder</ansi>

The Pathfinder is the good elite of the Scout (rogue route, alignment +30 at
promotion). It keeps the Scout's Ambush and Opening Strike and adds
reconnaissance: fewer ambushes against the company, openings on foes that have
not acted yet, and a company that starts its fights quicker. (The walking
skill is a different page: <ansi fg="command">help pathfinder</ansi>.)

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Pathfinder's Eye  enemy ambushes on the company happen half as
                       often, and Opening Strike opens one foe that has
                       not acted yet each battle
  35 Expose Weakness   an Opening Strike that hits leaves the target
                       exposed for 2 rounds
  40 Scouted ground    every ally's action meter starts the battle 10
                       points higher, and each acts a little earlier in
                       the first round (<ansi fg="command">help tempo</ansi>)
  45 Vanish            once a battle, when struck below 30% health, it
                       has +20 Evasion for the rest of that round and
                       the next
  50 Double opening    Pathfinder's Eye opens a foe that has not acted
                       yet twice a battle
  55 Trailwise         the cache a won random encounter leaves holds
                       15% more gold and is 10 points likelier to hold
                       equipment
  60 Ambush Master     when an ambush would catch the company off
                       guard, the company ambushes instead

Eye and Ambush Master work for the whole company while a living Pathfinder is
with it in the room. A battle says who spotted the ambush. Meter points speed
up a turn; they never grant an extra one. Everything here lasts only for the
battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Rogue elite talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Shadow Footing (+5 Evasion), Razor's
Edge (+5% critical chance), Quick Hands (+15 opening action meter). Every
elite rogue may take them. See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.


See also: <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help rogue-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help ambush</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help abilities</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
